# What Docker may copy into an image when it builds from the repo root.
# We use an ALLOW LIST: ignore everything first, then allow only what agents need.
# Safest for secrets: a .env file can never slip into an image by accident.

# 1. Ignore everything...
*

# 2. ...then allow just these:
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!agents/

# 3. ...but never these, even inside agents/:
**/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.md
